 "summary": "The conjugate layer is definitionally gUg\u207b\u00b9 \u25c1 gVg\u207b\u00b9 (membership `g\u207b\u00b9xg \u2208 U`), the Galois and level isomorphisms act by u \u21a6 gug\u207b\u00b9 and x \u21a6 \u03c1 g x with the correct intertwining identity, and the cohomology/Tate isomorphisms are Mathlib's `groupCohomology.mapIso` and `TateCohomology.mapIso` along that compatible pair, pinned in degree zero to the action of `g` on the ground level and on norm quotients. The action laws (`conjugate_one`, `conjugate_conjugate`, and the transported laws on Gal, norm quotient, ordinary and Tate cohomology) are non-vacuous and stated with the correct order `g * h`; the round's docstring clarification is accurate.",
